license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
type: software
abstract: >
  Lyceum is a fully-local multimodal system that ingests a static
  mathematics or statistics PDF textbook and turns it into an
  interactive, narrated whiteboard.  An offline pass builds a per-book
  math semantic graph that captures every formula, variable, concept
  and dependency before any narration starts; at run time, an
  orchestrator queries the graph per spoken clause and emits a small
  vocabulary of typed visual primitives (passage cards, book figures,
  curated canonical diagrams, formula cards, reference cards and
  cross-section connectors) timed against the audio clock.  A
  three-tier quality-assurance suite audits every ingested book and a
  self-healing loop repairs OCR-degraded formulas against the source
  PDF.  No external API is reachable from any production process.
keywords:
  - intelligent tutoring
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - multimodal narration
  - local LLM
  - vision-language inspection
  - math semantic graph
  - deterministic SVG synthesis
  - educational technology
  - mathematics textbook
  - audio-visual synchronisation
